## goal
Implement `memory-engine` for HTML-first generation of `/proyectos/[id]/memoria.html` from `input.json` + `resultados.json` + `spec.json`, covering contract, sectioned rendering, per-section templates, shared/section CSS, local asset staging, KaTeX/LaTeX hybrid traces, branded cover, HTML+print-ready index, hybrid theory section, always-visible alternatives, placeholder images, and working integration for `proyectos/1`.

## assumptions
- Source of truth = `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-23-memory-engine-design.md`.
- No `pdd/memory-engine/explore` or `pdd/memory-engine/requirements` artifacts exist; plan grounded on spec + repo evidence.
- Existing upstream artifacts are stable enough for v1: `proyectos/1/input.json`, `proyectos/1/resultados.json`, `proyectos/1/spec.json`.
- `lib/spec-engine/catalog/models.json` image paths are canonical source for equipment image references when staging project-local assets.
- Repo pattern should mirror current engines: pure helpers under `lib/memory-engine/` + thin runner/integration layer.
- Since no Engram tool is available in harness, persisted artifact lives at `pdd/memory-engine/plan` using requested topic key semantics.

## constraints
- Exclude final PDF generation, advanced pagination, alternate themes, visual template editors.
- Keep output HTML-first: exactly one generated artifact in scope, `/proyectos/[id]/memoria.html`.
- HTML must reference only project-local staged assets under `/proyectos/[id]/assets/`.
- Missing images/logos must not abort render; use placeholder/fallback.
- Formula policy fixed: structured trace -> KaTeX/LaTeX when possible, else human trace fallback.
- Alternatives policy fixed: always show if present, not only on failure.
- Theory policy fixed: hybrid static explanation + project-specific inserts.

